Now rebuild, and write a tmp Playwright test. Actually let me use a small node script in /home/runner/hub-work/noir-3d/tmp/e2e.mjs that imports playwright-core from the repo node_modules. I'll run it with cwd repo so import resolves.

Script:
```js
import { chromium } from 'playwright-core'
const exe='/usr/bin/chromium'
const browser = await chromium.launch({executablePath:exe,args:['--no-sandbox','--use-gl=angle','--use-angle=swiftshader','--enable-unsafe-swiftshader','--disable-dev-shm-usage']})
const page=await browser.newPage({viewport:{width:960,height:540}})
const logs=[]; page.on('pageerror',e=>logs.push('ERR '+e.message)); page.on('console',m=>{if(m.type()==='error')logs.push('CERR '+m.text())})
await page.goto('http://127.0.0.1:4173/?scene=game&nopost=1&dpr=1&camdebug=1&autostart=1',{waitUntil:'load',timeout:60000})
await page.waitForFunction('window.__ready===true',null,{timeout:180000})
await page.waitForTimeout(1500)
console.log('after start title:', await page.title())
// read body HUD text
const txt = await page.evaluate(()=>document.body.innerText)
console.log('HUD:', JSON.stringify(txt.slice(0,300)))
// count clues? 
const t0 = Date.now()
const title1 = await page.title()
// press W for 2 seconds
await page.keyboard.down('KeyW')
await page.waitForTimeout(2000)
await page.keyboard.up('KeyW')
await page.waitForTimeout(300)
console.log('after move title:', await page.title())
console.log('logs:', logs.slice(0,10))
await browser.close()
```

Wait: window.__ready is set by RenderProbe after a few frames regardless of phase. Good. autostart sets phase playing.

But camdebug writes title every frame, overriding RenderProbe maybe. RenderProbe sets title only if probe. Fine.

Let me rebuild and run.

